+# v31 revision notes
+
+## Why this revision exists
+
+The v30 instructions still left the user with a placeholder replay path and no concrete way to produce a replay CSV. v31 fixes that by adding an automated replay-construction layer.
+
+## Pipeline fixes
+
+- Added `os_cmasp.berth1_replay_adapter`.
+- Added `--write-synthetic-replay` to `berth1_conflict.py`.
+- Added a no-manual replay demo: `scripts/run_berth1_locked_replay_demo.sh`.
+- Added wide-export conversion: `scripts/build_berth1_replay_from_wide.sh`.
+- Added long-replay validation: `scripts/validate_berth1_replay_csv.sh`.
+- Hardened `scripts/run_berth1_replay.sh` against placeholder paths.
+- Hardened `scripts/package_results.sh` against empty result zips.
+- Added `data/examples/berth1_wide_example.csv`.
+
+## Paper revisions
+
+- Clarified that replay rows should be generated by scripts, not hand-edited from a template.
+- Added a main-paper subsection on automated replay construction.
+- Added a scaffold-smoke interpretation paragraph that uses the uploaded synthetic smoke output as a software sanity check, not as maritime evidence.
+- Tightened the validation language around what is and is not evidence.
+
+## Current evidence status
+
+The uploaded synthetic smoke run passes the locked active-regime checks. This supports the software scaffold and the separation pattern in the locked synthetic bank, but it is not maritime-twin evidence.
