+Replace synthetic claims with a replay CSV exported from the maritime twin. The replay schema must include episode identifier, step, visible-context features, latent readiness or admissibility label if available for evaluation, observer, situation, assertion, timestamp, credibility, provenance, and intervention outcome. The solver and ablation interface remain unchanged. A replay path must be an actual file; placeholder paths such as \texttt{path/to/twin\_replay\_claims.csv} are documentation only. \emph{Replay rows should not be created by hand-editing the template}. The template is a schema contract. A run should either validate an existing long-form replay export or use an adapter that converts a one-row-per-step twin export into the canonical one-row-per-claim replay table. This distinction is operationally important: manual template editing can accidentally change the claim bank, while the paper's ablation requires the same episode bank across all conditions.
 
